{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788219053225353024,"compiled_state":{"alias":"watertight-sirenian-auk","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":7,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"214179748a75ef814bebd8ad97f13f5f5ddf930759c60438d945f21eaf3c2a4b","event_uuid":"835388bc-7245-4cb7-ae39-3bdac93a99dc","position":{"commit_sha":"77ae5e16af67fef5f49732c0b9998e302ba5debe","position":"1788217723231066060-835388bc-7245-4cb7-ae39-3bdac93a99dc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"dede1e0b43174c44b960baf1c4c9304d1a6806fcf6b924cd4f449c5b081e7fef","event_uuid":"3ca47d4c-19eb-4600-8f6d-c83daf09d9fd","position":{"commit_sha":"02e9daec33f4100f44947c7cd9ea5a5820182746","position":"1788217781274656590-3ca47d4c-19eb-4600-8f6d-c83daf09d9fd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"1b088894ff7c1dd3b3887f2d2c1ed8cabd1f619a6d40701ef77f7b9b4b0ce60c","event_uuid":"dbd3eacf-e612-467d-a19e-d2308a1c0ba2","position":{"commit_sha":"422637147e0edf268905d16a64aad695d1edfc94","position":"1788217794436213930-dbd3eacf-e612-467d-a19e-d2308a1c0ba2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"48849876de2663feff953feab805b4dd15c825d25319dd58022f8df8f0bb01c5","event_uuid":"e920f7b0-ce3f-4410-99ef-cfc380a09e2c","position":{"commit_sha":"ce918f2302d911251099f769524f917aa460f03d","position":"1788218332610351206-e920f7b0-ce3f-4410-99ef-cfc380a09e2c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"b7bda63023250b279cf15cce660cb502a165f9ba598092647f0b5dac0029edc4","event_uuid":"a3d0b79b-1710-4baa-a5e6-c7d504cb8f18","position":{"commit_sha":"79220af3845cee7516d61de1d20aa7434c0471aa","position":"1788219053206656536-a3d0b79b-1710-4baa-a5e6-c7d504cb8f18"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"7992fef91c24a4d1377e62b887fd3e9d23f66daa06af96b32b5ab372c9937fb7","event_uuid":"c32db391-4f87-4966-8891-ac2969f5ca1e","position":{"commit_sha":"e175bec953079203c427203898590b231b42ad5f","position":"1788219053216183662-c32db391-4f87-4966-8891-ac2969f5ca1e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"9e4216b84792c00b3967e68b75d0eeab74cad0a34bf72429e031cfd82be383b8","event_uuid":"b10f3deb-0b64-4750-b0ac-a25e0dd768fc","position":{"commit_sha":"7e3a63df05cdce4cbe4c3b00cc49e25938522cb7","position":"1788219053225353023-b10f3deb-0b64-4750-b0ac-a25e0dd768fc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 legitimacy checkpoint (rebar-debug): confirmed the reported mechanism locally by setting `rebar._store.git_locking.fcntl = None`; entering `_store_git_op_lock` and `fetch_coordination_lock` both raises `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'flock'`, matching CI run 33426859481 (`git_locking.py:224` via `_with_index_lock_retry`). However, the repository currently contains an authoritative contrary scope statement in `scripts/check_fcntl_import_guard.py:19-20`: “actually *using* `fcntl` off POSIX is out of scope — Windows is not a declared support target — only that import/collection succeeds.” The commit that added the import guard (5697f2e11179 / ticket 0b31-aeb5-e734-41c9) says the same: “Collectability only; making fcntl locking work on Windows stays out of scope (not a declared support target).” Per the reporter’s explicit guard, this makes the no-fcntl runtime-lock repair a design/support-scope decision rather than an auto-fixable defect. I am not changing production locking code or using force; escalation required to decide whether Windows runtime lock usage is now supported.","timestamp":1788218332610351206},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Correction: an earlier Phase 1 legitimacy comment on this ticket described the separate `fcntl.flock` Windows failure and belongs to `oxymoronic-industrial-wrasse`. The RCA for THIS ticket is the Windows env-var limit in pytest’s `PYTEST_CURRENT_TEST`: run 33426859481 fails at `_pytest.runner._update_current_test_var` while setting a nodeid containing the 60,000-character `far_over_limit` parameter from `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_outbound_comment_marker_survives_truncation.py`. Local measurement before repair: collected nodeids are 60,163 chars for `far_over_limit` and 75,169 chars for `over_limit_multiline`; simulating the Windows cap raises the same `ValueError` at 60,171 chars. Legitimacy: test-harness defect; product input remains large, only pytest's generated id is unsafe. Attribution: commit 6724e79e8ff857b54dd36a62006a89445fc10ad6 / ticket 5931-78a3-95d2-44cd added the long parametrization without explicit short ids.","timestamp":1788219053206656536}],"created_at":1788217723231066060,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Problem\nThe scheduled Test Suite (mirror) Windows sweep reports `ValueError: the environment variable is longer than 32767 characters` in two tests around run 33426859481. Windows caps each environment variable at 32767 characters; some test or subprocess helper appears to pass an oversized payload through `env`.\n\n## Plan\n1. Inspect the failing CI log and identify the exact tests/helpers setting the long environment variable.\n2. Classify legitimacy: if this is a test-harness-only payload transport, fix the harness to pass large data via a file/stdin/in-process seam; if it is a product path a real Windows user can hit, fix the product path. Escalate if an authoritative design says this behavior is intentional.\n3. Add a RED test that simulates the Windows env-var cap deterministically on macOS and fails for the same `ValueError` mechanism before the fix.\n4. Apply the smallest fix that avoids oversized Windows env vars without weakening test coverage or adding dependencies.\n5. Run the focused test, sandboxed mutation check, `make lint`, and the default suite before Gerrit.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The exact failing tests/helpers from run 33426859481 are identified in the RCA.\n- [ ] A local macOS test simulates the Windows 32767-character env-var cap and is RED on current code for the right reason.\n- [ ] The fixed path avoids passing oversized payloads through a single environment variable.\n- [ ] The RCA comment cites the legitimacy verdict, caller/sibling sweep, and caused-by attribution.\n- [ ] Gerrit change is submitted only after `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_outbound_comment_marker_survives_truncation.py","reason":"Add short pytest parameter ids and a Windows PYTEST_CURRENT_TEST length regression assertion."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["navapbc/rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["ci","windows","debugging"],"ticket_id":"b4f5-11c0-8633-4204","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep hits 32767-character environment variable limit in tests","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["835388bc-7245-4cb7-ae39-3bdac93a99dc","3ca47d4c-19eb-4600-8f6d-c83daf09d9fd","dbd3eacf-e612-467d-a19e-d2308a1c0ba2","e920f7b0-ce3f-4410-99ef-cfc380a09e2c","a3d0b79b-1710-4baa-a5e6-c7d504cb8f18","c32db391-4f87-4966-8891-ac2969f5ca1e","b10f3deb-0b64-4750-b0ac-a25e0dd768fc"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788219053225353024,"uuid":"ab89e3e5-ce1c-4da2-abbe-723da6b2d9ba"}